---
// The moving parts and how they talk, drawn with FabricUI's tokens so it reads in light and dark alike
---

<figure class="figure arch">
  <div class="scroll">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 560" role="img" aria-labelledby="arch-title arch-desc">
      <title id="arch-title">FeedFabric's architecture</title>
      <desc id="arch-desc">
        Your identity provider issues tokens to your app and the admin panel, which call FeedFabric.Api over REST. The
        API reads and writes Redis, PostgreSQL and blob storage. FeedFabric.Worker.Events publishes the Postgres outbox
        to Kafka, consumes it, and updates Redis timelines, scans photos with ClamAV and writes blobs. The ml folder
        trains the ranker from the feed log in Postgres and publishes ONNX models to blob storage. The simulator uses
        the same services against the same Postgres and Redis.
      </desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="arch-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" class="head" />
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <!-- Callers -->
      <g class="box"><rect x="20" y="20" width="210" height="70" rx="10" /><text x="125" y="50">Identity provider</text><text x="125" y="72" class="sub">Auth0, Entra ID, Keycloak…</text></g>
      <g class="box you"><rect x="20" y="150" width="210" height="80" rx="10" /><text x="125" y="182">Your app</text><text x="125" y="206" class="sub">your member UI</text></g>
      <g class="box"><rect x="20" y="270" width="210" height="70" rx="10" /><text x="125" y="300">Admin panel</text><text x="125" y="322" class="sub">web/admin · staff only</text></g>
      <g class="box dashed"><rect x="20" y="400" width="210" height="80" rx="10" /><text x="125" y="432">Simulator</text><text x="125" y="454" class="sub">1,000 simulated members</text></g>

      <!-- FeedFabric -->
      <g class="box"><rect x="300" y="20" width="260" height="70" rx="10" /><text x="430" y="50">ml/train_ranker.py</text><text x="430" y="72" class="sub">LightGBM → ONNX</text></g>
      <g class="box core">
        <rect x="300" y="150" width="260" height="190" rx="12" />
        <text x="430" y="182">FeedFabric.Api</text>
        <text x="430" y="208" class="sub">/userfeed /follows</text>
        <text x="430" y="228" class="sub">/favourites /media</text>
        <text x="430" y="248" class="sub">/admin /ranking (staff)</text>
        <text x="430" y="278" class="sub">text moderation</text>
        <text x="430" y="298" class="sub">For You ranking</text>
        <text x="430" y="318" class="sub">feed log and signals</text>
      </g>
      <g class="box core">
        <rect x="300" y="390" width="260" height="140" rx="12" />
        <text x="430" y="422">FeedFabric.Worker.Events</text>
        <text x="430" y="450" class="sub">outbox → Kafka</text>
        <text x="430" y="472" class="sub">fan-out · engagement</text>
        <text x="430" y="494" class="sub">photo checks · embeddings</text>
      </g>

      <!-- State and infrastructure -->
      <g class="group"><rect x="640" y="20" width="340" height="520" rx="14" /><text x="660" y="46">State and infrastructure</text></g>
      <g class="box store"><rect x="660" y="62" width="300" height="62" rx="9" /><text x="810" y="88">Redis</text><text x="810" y="109" class="sub">timelines, For You sessions, signals</text></g>
      <g class="box store"><rect x="660" y="140" width="300" height="62" rx="9" /><text x="810" y="166">PostgreSQL</text><text x="810" y="187" class="sub">posts, users, FeedLog, outbox</text></g>
      <g class="box store"><rect x="660" y="218" width="300" height="62" rx="9" /><text x="810" y="244">Blob storage</text><text x="810" y="265" class="sub">photos and ONNX models (disk or S3)</text></g>
      <g class="box store"><rect x="660" y="380" width="300" height="62" rx="9" /><text x="810" y="406">Kafka</text><text x="810" y="427" class="sub">posts · engagement · media topics</text></g>
      <g class="box store"><rect x="660" y="458" width="300" height="62" rx="9" /><text x="810" y="484">ClamAV</text><text x="810" y="505" class="sub">malware scan (switchable)</text></g>

      <!-- Arrows -->
      <g class="line">
        <path d="M125 90V150" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)" />
        <path d="M230 190H300" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)" />
        <path d="M230 305H300" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)" />
        <path d="M560 245H640" marker-start="url(#arch-arrow)" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)" />
        <path d="M560 460H640" marker-start="url(#arch-arrow)" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)" />
        <path d="M560 55H640" marker-start="url(#arch-arrow)" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)" />
        <path d="M125 480V550H810V542" class="dashed" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)" />
      </g>
      <g class="label">
        <text x="135" y="124" text-anchor="start">token</text>
        <text x="265" y="182">REST</text>
        <text x="265" y="297">REST</text>
        <text x="600" y="234">reads,</text><text x="600" y="266">writes</text>
        <text x="600" y="452">consumes</text>
        <text x="600" y="44">FeedLog</text><text x="600" y="76">ONNX</text>
        <text x="470" y="554">same services, same Postgres and Redis</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <p class="hint" aria-hidden="true">Scroll sideways to see the whole diagram.</p>
  <figcaption>
    Your app only ever talks to the API. Everything slow or fan-shaped (timelines, counters, photo checks, embeddings)
    happens in the worker, driven by events the API writes to Postgres in the same transaction as the change.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .arch svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 680px; height: auto; font-family: var(--fabric-font); }
  .arch .box rect { fill: var(--fabric-surface-raised); stroke: var(--fabric-line-strong); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .arch .box.you rect { fill: var(--fabric-good-soft); stroke: var(--fabric-good); }
  .arch .box.core rect { fill: var(--fabric-accent-soft); stroke: var(--fabric-accent); }
  .arch .box.store rect { fill: var(--fabric-surface); }
  .arch .box.dashed rect { stroke-dasharray: 6 5; }
  .arch .box text { fill: var(--fabric-ink); font-size: 18px; font-weight: 650; text-anchor: middle; }
  .arch .box text.sub { fill: var(--fabric-muted); font-size: 15px; font-weight: 450; }
  .arch .group rect { fill: var(--fabric-sunken); stroke: var(--fabric-line); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .arch .group text { fill: var(--fabric-muted); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .arch .line path { fill: none; stroke: var(--fabric-muted); stroke-width: 1.6; }
  .arch .line path.dashed { stroke-dasharray: 5 5; }
  .arch .head { fill: var(--fabric-muted); }
  .arch .label text { fill: var(--fabric-muted); font-size: 14px; text-anchor: middle; paint-order: stroke; stroke: var(--fabric-surface); stroke-width: 4px; }
</style>
